        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "31e2a853-61ab-55cb-8dba-01ae24ebc75f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Wyler, Audrey Hepburn, Peter O'Toole, Eli Wallach, Hugh Griffith, Nicole Bonnet\n- Works: How to Steal a Million, Papa and Nicole\n- Organizations: Royal Academy of Dramatic Art, Bristol Old Vic\n- Topics: film careers, adaptation in advertisements\n\nFacts:\n- In 1959, Peter O'Toole made his film debut after attending the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art and gaining recognition as a Shakespearean actor at the Bristol Old Vic and in theatre.\n- In 1966, How to Steal a Million was released as a heist comedy film directed by William Wyler.\n- In 1966, How to Steal a Million starred Audrey Hepburn, Peter O'Toole, Eli Wallach, and Hugh Griffith.\n- In How to Steal a Million, Audrey Hepburn played Nicole Bonnet and Hugh Griffith played her father.\n- Papa and Nicole adapted verbal exchanges used in its advertisements from an original exchange between Nicole Bonnet and her father in the 1966 film How to Steal a Million.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5f94d032-db22-5a9b-9e1e-7c00a7260ffe",
